course: dictionary
lesson: 4452
title: Names that are not ordinary words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Most words in a dictionary are ordinary words, like hungry or river. Some words are names, and names are different. «The Hani people in Yunnan built rice terraces up whole mountains.» Hani is not an ordinary English word. It is the name of a people, so it starts with a capital letter.
explain: A name can be for a people, a language, a place, or a person. Hani is the name of a people of southern China, Vietnam, Laos and Myanmar. Their language is also called Hani. Hani can also be a first name in Arabic and some other languages, and a surname.
explain: When you see a word with a capital letter in the middle of a sentence, ask: is this a name? Look at the words around it for clues, like «the Hani rice terraces». If it is a name, you do not look for its meaning in an ordinary way. You learn who or what it names.
fact: A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place, people or thing.
fact: Proper nouns always begin with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence.
fact: «Hani» is the name of a people of southern China, Vietnam, Laos and Myanmar.
fact: The Hani language is also called Hani.
fact: «Hani» can also be a first name or a surname, for example in Arabic.
exercise: «Hani rice terraces are carved into mountain slopes.» Which word is a name? | terraces | rice | *Hani | slopes
exercise: Why does «Hani» start with a capital H? | Because it is the most important word on the page | Because it is a long word | Because it comes at the start of every sentence | *Because it is a name
exercise: «The Hani people in Yunnan built rice terraces over about 1,300 years.» Where do the Hani people live? | *Southern China, Vietnam, Laos and Myanmar | In a desert with no water | Only in London | On the moon
test: «The Hani language is spoken by the Hani people.» What does Hani mean here? | *The name of a people and of their language | A type of rice | A kind of food | A kind of mountain
test: Hani is used as a first name in Arabic. How should you write it at the start of a name? | hani | Hani with a small h | HANI in brackets | *Hani with a capital H
exam: «The Honghe Hani rice terraces in Yunnan are a UNESCO World Heritage Site.» Why is Hani written with a capital H? | *Because it is part of a name | Because the sentence is important | Because it is written in a book | Because it is the first word of the sentence
